  "limitations": [
    "Smoke/dust from source states has been stripped where detached; some baked-in effects still overlap the vehicle silhouette.",
    "The frames are resized from illustrated source art; close-up sprites can have antialiasing in the color even with binary alpha.",
    "There are only four static key states per vehicle, not functional wheel/rotor cycles or independently layered parts.",
    "Guard pilot anchors are approximate, require actual 320x180 gameplay integration QA."
  ],
  "implementation_direction": [
    "Create each vehicle as independent physics actor with specified hitbox/pivot; separate driver guard character layer.",
    "Use vehicle right and left keys as orientation references; no automatic flip for asymmetric insignias until QA.",
    "For full animations, add independent wheel/rotor overlays and damage/dust VFX layers; source itself does not supply cycle.",
    "Guard response/wanted escalation still requires existing successful reporting/signal paths. Do not spawn vehicles on unreported sight alone.",
    "While in pursuit, vehicles may chase across authored connected areas where geometry supports it and faction collisions are allowed."
  ]
